  <releases>
    <release version="1.0.15" date="2026-10-26">
      <description>
        <p>More painting and editing tools on Windows.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Edit vector layers and blend paint with new brush controls.</li>
          <li>Float tools in bubbles and restore your workspace between sessions.</li>
          <li>Try artistic filters and improved mask, color and number controls.</li>
          <li>Recover the canvas after graphics errors and keep tools responsive.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.0.14" date="2026-10-19">
      <description>
        <p>Redesigned pencils, charcoal, chalk, pastels and crayons respond to pressure, tilt and paper.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Choose built-in papers or import textures, with adjustable lighting.</li>
          <li>Calibrate pen pressure and set smoothing for each brush.</li>
          <li>Create drawings with physical units and searchable presets.</li>
          <li>Native Windows Arm64 and iPadOS 17.5+ support.</li>
          <li>Sketch combines Layers and Properties in one drawer.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.0.12" date="2026-10-09">
      <description>
        <p>Copy and paste selected areas, layers and masks, or paste into a new drawing. Zoom, Hand, Rotate, recovery and Safari startup improve.</p>
        <p>Imported and pasted images keep original pixels in Object layers until Rasterize Layer.</p>
        <p>This beta changes the Object-layer format. Earlier Object-layer drawings cannot be edited in this version. Before updating, export flattened PNG copies and keep original drawing files.</p>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.0.11" date="2026-10-07">
      <description>
        <p>This maintenance release improves Android downloads and delivery of test builds.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Android downloads pass the latest Google Play signature checks.</li>
          <li>Verified Android builds reach internal testers before closed-beta review.</li>
          <li>iPad test builds reuse the signing identity for future updates.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.0.10" date="2026-10-07">
      <description>
        <p>Android downloads open without requiring installation through Google Play.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Android updates keep the signing identity of existing installations.</li>
          <li>The app name follows your language on supported platforms.</li>
          <li>Title bar spacing follows the selected control size.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.0.9" date="2026-10-06">
      <description>
        <p>The Linux battery indicator works without access to system services.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Flatpak installations no longer request access to UPower.</li>
          <li>The battery indicator reads system batteries in the background and excludes connected accessories.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.0.8" date="2026-10-06">
      <description>
        <p>Linux software centers now show Capy Canvas in your language, with light and dark previews.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Saving a read-only drawing opens a chooser so you can save an editable copy.</li>
          <li>The battery indicator and clock follow your desktop in Flatpak installations.</li>
          <li>Translated Histogram controls fit their labels.</li>
          <li>Drawings with filters reopen correctly after restarting the app.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.0.6" date="2026-10-05">
      <description>
        <p>Capy Canvas is available as a Flatpak for Linux.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Open the downloaded Flatpak installer in your software manager to install Capy Canvas.</li>
          <li>Flatpak installations receive signed updates through your software manager.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.0.4" date="2026-10-05">
      <description>
        <p>A small update for Windows.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The Windows uninstaller is signed, like the app and its setup program.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.0.3" date="2026-10-04">
      <description>
        <p>The first public beta of Capy Canvas, for Linux, Windows, macOS, iPad, Android tablets and the web.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Enclose and Fill, under Lasso Fill, fills the empty areas inside a loop you draw.</li>
          <li>Edit Color has a new layout on Windows, macOS and iPad, with color values you can type, drag to adjust and copy.</li>
          <li>On macOS and iPad, tap a color fill's thumbnail, Paper included, to change its color.</li>
          <li>Layer thumbnails have rounded corners everywhere, and filters use the same effects icon throughout.</li>
          <li>Windows reopens all your windows at launch and asks about any drawing it could not restore.</li>
          <li>The Windows color wheel stays smooth while panels resize, and Export Preview on Windows works again.</li>
          <li>The Windows app and setup program are signed, and the Mac app is notarized by Apple.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.0.2" date="2026-10-04" />
    <release version="1.0.1" date="2026-10-04" />
    <release version="1.0.0" date="2026-10-04" />
  </releases>
